      "key": "app_stack_dependencies",
      "role": "system",
      "content": "**Guided Review** — Tauri 2 desktop app (identifier `co.garden.guided-review`) for section-by-section GitHub PR review via ACP-compatible agents (Claude Code or Codex via npx).\n- **Frontend**: React 19 + Vite 6 + TypeScript ~5.7 (strict, ES2022, @/ import alias). Tailwind v4 (@tailwindcss/vite plugin). Zustand 5 (single store). Radix UI primitives (dialog, dropdown-menu, slot). @pierre/diffs (diff rendering in-browser). lucide-react icons, react-markdown + remark-gfm, cmdk, class-variance-authority, clsx, tailwind-merge.\n- **Backend (Rust)**: Tauri 2 + tokio (rt-multi-thread, process, sync, fs, io-util). git2 v0.19 (vendored-libgit2). agent-client-protocol v0.11 (ACP JSON-RPC). serde + serde_json + schemars + json5 (lenient parse fallback). uuid, url, dirs, shell-words, async-process, futures, tokio-util.\n- **Telemetry**: OpenTelemetry (Rust SDK + web SDK). OTLP HTTP/binary (default http://127.0.0.1:54418). Rust service: guided-review-app. Frontend: guided-review-app-client. \n- **DB**: libsql (review state persistence).\n- **Build/test**: tsc --noEmit (check), tsx --test for TS unit tests, cargo test for Rust. Vite dev on port 1421.\n- **Release**: local-release.mjs (macOS universal-apple-darwin: .dmg + .app.tar.gz + .sig). GitHub Actions release.yml (manual trigger). npm run bump-version ({patch|minor|major|x.y.z}).\n- **Prerequisites**: Node.js + npm, Rust/Cargo stable, git + gh CLI, Tauri system deps.",
      "category": "dependencies",
      "ttlDays": 30,
      "updatedAt": "2026-05-21T10:48:54.382Z",
      "source": "context_agent"
    },
    {
      "key": "review_session_flow",
      "role": "system",
      "content": "## Main user flow\n1. **Project picker** → user selects local repo folder (or enters PR/branch/SHA without clone)\n2. **PR input** → user enters GitHub PR number or URL; repo guard rejects mismatched owner/repo\n3. **Agent selection** → user picks ACP agent (Claude Code / Codex), listed via `list_agents_cmd`\n4. **Session start** → `start_session_cmd` resolves source (clone if needed via git2), fetches PR metadata + existing review comments via `gh`, spawns agent via npx (login-shell PATH resolution), returns session_id\n5. **Kickoff** → UI sends agent-skill.md + repo info to agent; agent emits `acp-section-map` (fenced JSON block)\n6. **Section enrichment** → `enrichSectionMapWithLocalRanges` fetches changed line ranges from local git per section\n7. **Section walkthrough** → user clicks a section → `start_section_task_cmd` → agent analyzes (optionally delegates to sub-agent) → emits `acp-section` with concerns\n8. **Chat** → user can converse per-section; `acp://text-chunk` events streamed to chat panel; structured blocks stripped from display\n9. **Comment drafts** → user asks agent → emits `acp-comment-draft`; user approves/rejects in UI\n10. **Publishing** → user approves drafts → host sends prompt to agent via `buildAgentPublishCommentPrompt` → agent publishes via its own `gh` auth → emits `acp-comment-result`\n\n## Key events (acp:// namespace)\n- `acp://section-map`, `acp://section`, `acp://section-progress` — review structure\n- `acp://text-chunk`, `acp://turn-done` — chat streaming\n- `acp://comment-draft`, `acp://comment-result` — PR comment lifecycle\n- `acp://tool-call-update`, `acp://error`, `acp://agent-stderr`, `acp://pr-description`\n\n## Auto-behaviors\n- First section auto-opened after section map arrives (intentional UX override of agent-skill.md)\n- Next section auto-loads when current section finishes processing\n- `pr_description` synthetic section stays selected until user clicks another\n- Session state persisted to libsql on change (debounced 500ms)",
      "category": "flow_logic",
      "ttlDays": 30,
      "updatedAt": "2026-05-21T10:48:54.382Z",
      "source": "context_agent"
    },
    {
      "key": "code_conventions_and_rules",
      "role": "system",
      "content": "## TypeScript conventions\n- **Tab indentation** (enforced by existing files, do not switch to spaces)\n- **Strict mode** on (noUnusedLocals, noUnusedParameters, noFallthroughCasesInSwitch)\n- **No default exports** for components — named exports only\n- **Import alias**: `@/` → `src/` (configured in vite.config.ts + tsconfig.json)\n- **Wire types**: snake_case on wire; TS interfaces mirror Rust serde. Use `tag = \"kind\"` for discriminated unions (see SessionSource, RecentProject)\n- **Single Zustand store** (`src/lib/store.ts`) — components read only, App.tsx mutates via event subscribers\n\n## Rust conventions\n- `anyhow::Result` at public boundaries; errors surfaced to UI as `String` via `.map_err(|e| e.to_string())`\n- `tracing::instrument` on async commands; span parents wired from TelemetryContext\n- Snake_case for everything; serde rename for camelCase where needed\n\n## Critical non-obvious rules (read before changing)\n- **Fenced parser is lenient**: `fenced.rs::parse_lenient` tries serde_json first, then json5. Mirror this for new block tags.\n- **Streaming overlap dedup**: `acp_client.rs::shared_boundary_len` (Rust) and `store.ts::appendStreamingText` (TS) are paired implementations — keep them in sync. Both detect agents that replay assembled prefix.\n- **Structured blocks stripped from chat**: `store.ts::stripStructuredReviewBlocks` removes fenced acp-* blocks from visible text. Don't re-add them.\n- **Tool-call payloads as alternative section channels**: `App.tsx::handleToolCall` inspects raw_input for section map / review section shapes — some agents emit these as tool args.\n- **Permission requests auto-approve**: OK because sandbox is user's machine and agent already has shell access.\n- **Nested-agent env scrubbing**: `acp_client.rs::scrub_nested_agent_env` removes CLAUDECODE*/CLAUDE_CODE_*/CODEX_*/ACP_* before spawning. Extend prefix list if adding new agent kinds.\n- **Comment publishing delegated to agent** — host has no GitHub credentials. Never publish comments from Rust code.\n- **Don't paste diffs or file contents into agent replies** — host renders them. Reference via LineRange.\n- **Not a Vercel/Next.js project** — ignore plugin hints that assume otherwise.\n\n## Testing patterns\n- Unit tests colocated: `src/**/*.test.ts` (tsx --test), `scripts/*.test.mjs` (node --test)\n- Rust tests: `cd src-tauri && cargo test`\n- No end-to-end test framework — manual testing via `npm run tauri -- dev` against real PR\n- `npm run check` = tsc --noEmit (must pass before PR)",
      "category": "code_rules",
      "ttlDays": 30,
      "updatedAt": "2026-05-21T10:48:54.382Z",
      "source": "context_agent"
    },
    {
      "key": "file_map_and_architecture",
      "role": "system",
      "content": "## Frontend (src/)\n- **`src/main.tsx`** — Entry point: inits telemetry, renders App\n- **`src/App.tsx`** — Single subscriber for acp://* events; wires all event handlers to Zustand store. Start here for UI event flow changes.\n- **`src/lib/store.ts`** — Single Zustand store (AppState). All state mutations happen here. 1200 lines — the heart of frontend logic.\n- **`src/lib/acp.ts`** — Typed wrapper over Tauri invoke() + listen(). Defines all event types and command interfaces.\n- **`src/lib/types/section.ts`** — Shared wire types (ReviewSection, SectionMap, CommentDraft, etc.)\n- **`src/lib/projectSource.ts`** — PR/branch/URL parsing, local-review-source validation, last-project persistence\n- **`src/lib/commentPublish.ts`** — Builds the prompt that asks agent to publish approved comment drafts\n- **`src/lib/telemetry.ts`** — Client-side OTel init and helpers\n- **`src/lib/reviewPersistence.ts`** — Review snapshot creation + save/restore via libsql on Rust side\n- **`src/lib/sectionQueue.ts`** — Auto-load logic for next section\n- **`src/lib/diffFocus.ts`** — Selected/referenced diff range tracking\n- **`src/lib/ghCli.ts`** — gh CLI status checking\n- **`src/components/`** — UI components: DiffView, ChatPanel, SectionList, ReviewLauncher, ProjectPicker, CommentDraftCard, Concerns, SeverityBadge, MarkdownViewer, plus ui/ subfolder (button, dialog, card, command, input, textarea, badge)\n\n## Backend (src-tauri/src/)\n- **`src-tauri/src/lib.rs`** — Tauri builder setup: registers all plugins and command handlers. Start here for new capabilities.\n- **`src-tauri/src/main.rs`** — Calls lib::run()\n- **`src-tauri/src/commands.rs`** — All #[tauri::command] entry points (16 commands). Contains prompt building logic for section tasks.\n- **`src-tauri/src/acp_client.rs`** — Spawns ACP agent (npx), runs turn loop via mpsc queue, handles streaming chunks, env scrubbing, shared_boundary_len dedup\n- **`src-tauri/src/agent_runner.rs`** — Resolves npx via login-shell PATH, agent discovery\n- **`src-tauri/src/fenced.rs`** — Buffers stdout chunks, extracts fenced acp-* blocks with lenient JSON parsing (serde_json → json5)\n- **`src-tauri/src/repo.rs`** — Git operations: clone, fetch, diff, file-at-ref, PR URL parsing, origin inspection\n- **`src-tauri/src/projects.rs`** — Recent-projects JSON store (~/Library/Application Support/…/recent.json, max 20)\n- **`src-tauri/src/review_persistence.rs`** — libsql-based save/restore of review state\n- **`src-tauri/src/events.rs`** — Tauri event name constants\n- **`src-tauri/src/section.rs`** — LineRange type\n- **`src-tauri/src/telemetry.rs`** — Rust OTel init and shutdown\n- **`src-tauri/src/gh.rs`** — GitHub CLI integration wrappers\n\n## Other important files\n- **`agent-skill.md`** — ACP agent contract (fenced block formats, workflow). Injected into every agent's first prompt.\n- **`scripts/bump-version.mjs`** — Version bumping utility\n- **`scripts/local-release.mjs`** — macOS release bundling + notarization\n- **`.github/workflows/release.yml`** — CI release workflow\n- **`src-tauri/tauri.conf.json`** — Tauri app config (window size 1280x800, CSP null, bundle targets)\n- **`src-tauri/Cargo.toml`** — Rust crate config (edition 2021, staticlib+cdylib+rlib)\n\n## Known gaps (from AGENTS.md)\n- `markSectionCompleted` exists but no caller fires it\n- `get_diff_cmd` exposed but unused (diff computed client-side by @pierre/diffs)\n- Agent-driven diffFocus (source:agent, mode:navigation) has UI plumbing but no event source\n- AgentStderrEvent.session_id always empty\n- schema_version from agent payloads always overwritten with 1 in fenced.rs",
      "category": "file_map",
      "ttlDays": 30,
      "updatedAt": "2026-05-21T10:48:54.382Z",
      "source": "context_agent"
    },
    {
      "key": "agent_protocol_contract",
      "role": "system",
      "content": "## ACP Agent Contract (agent-skill.md)\nThe agent (Claude Code or Codex) communicates via fenced JSON blocks in stdout:\n\n### Fenced block types\n- **`acp-section-map`** (first turn only): `{ \"sections\": [{ \"section_id\", \"title\", \"intent\", \"files\" }] }` — defines review structure. No ranges/base_ref/head_ref.\n- **`acp-section`** (per section): `{ \"section_id\", \"concerns\": [{ \"text\", \"severity\" (high|medium|low), \"file_path\", \"line\" }] }` — feedback only. No title/intent/files/ranges.\n- **`acp-comment-draft`**: `{ \"kind\" (inline|top_level), \"title\" (≤5 words), \"body\", \"file_path\", \"line\", \"side\" (LEFT|RIGHT) }`\n- **`acp-comment-result`**: `{ \"draft_id\", \"status\" (published|failed), \"url\"?, \"error\"? }`\n\n### Workflow rules\n1. One section per turn — always stop after each `acp-section`\n2. Section map first (including file lists), then wait for user\n3. Group sections by intent, not filename alone\n4. Agent must NOT paste diffs or file contents into replies — host renders them\n5. Agent can delegate per-section analysis to a sub-agent (Task tool). Parent performs false-positive check on sub-agent's output.\n6. Optional tool: `guided_review_update_section` (section_id, phase: started|feedback, concerns) — for progressive UI updates\n7. Concerns analyzed across 7 pillars: correctness, maintainability, readability, efficiency, security, edge cases & error handling, testability",
      "category": "flow_logic",
      "ttlDays": 30,
      "updatedAt": "2026-05-21T10:48:54.382Z",
      "source": "context_agent"
    },
    {
      "key": "review_persistence_and_state",
      "role": "system",
      "content": "## State persistence\n- **Review state** saved to libsql database via `save_review_state_cmd` (debounced 500ms in App.tsx useEffect). Restored on session resume via `saved_review` in StartSessionResponse.\n- **Recent projects** persisted to platform data dir (`recent.json`), max 20 entries, deduplicated by fingerprint.\n- **Cloned PR repos** (when source is Pr/Branch/Sha without local clone) stored under `<data_dir>/repos/<owner>-<repo>`.\n\n## Session lifecycle\n- `AcpSessions` (managed via tauri State) tracks all active agent processes. `shutdown_all()` called on ExitRequested.\n- Agent spawned via `$SHELL -lc 'npx ...'` after login-shell PATH resolution (agent_runner.rs).\n- Each section gets its own chat session (max 3 concurrent, LRU eviction) — `attachSectionChatSession` / `detachSectionChatSession` in store.\n\n## Telemetry\n- OTLP HTTP/binary to 127.0.0.1:54418 by default. Override with `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` (Rust) or `VITE_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` (frontend).\n- `GUIDED_REVIEW_CAPTURE_ASSISTANT_TEXT=1` enables agent chunk text logging in release builds (off by default).\n- All telemetry events prefixed with `client.` (frontend) or use tracing spans with OTel attributes (Rust).",
      "category": "code_rules",
      "ttlDays": 30,
      "updatedAt": "2026-05-21T10:48:54.382Z",
      "source": "context_agent"
    }
  ]
